- remove hash_algorithm enum and replace with hash function type: done
- remove partition_info::enum_key_algorithm and replace with a string-function pair struct: it introduces complexity because the existing mysql5x algorithms don't follow the same function interface, so didn't do
- no call to strnxfrm when using binary character sets: done by checking that the hash_sort algorithm is my_hash_sort_bin. Other my_hash_sort_*_bin functions have some transformations that can cause trouble

Question (also to myself): is 4096 as the size ok to use?
{code:diff}
+      uchar newstr[4096] = {'\0'};
+      const size_t newlen= cs->strnxfrm(newstr, 4096, str, length);
+      my_hash_dispatch(newstr, newlen, &m_nr, m_algo);
