                                                        ^~~~~
{noformat}

I think that the following code (which I understand is supposed to exist only for test purposes in special debug builds) should be disabled by default:
{code:cmake}
OPTION(WITH_INNODB_LEGACY_FOREIGN_STORAGE "Create SYS_FOREIGN, SYS_FOREIGN_COLS tables" ON)
IF (WITH_INNODB_LEGACY_FOREIGN_STORAGE)
  ADD_DEFINITIONS(-DWITH_INNODB_LEGACY_FOREIGN_STORAGE)
ENDIF()
{code}
Enabling that code by default undermines the purpose of the task, which is to phase out the InnoDB internal metadata storage for {{FOREIGN KEY}} constraints.

I would like to see a test case that exercises the upgrade logic. The following failed for me when I disabled the above:
{code:sql}
--source include/have_innodb.inc

CREATE TABLE parent(a INT PRIMARY KEY) ENGINE=InnoDB;
CREATE TABLE child(a INT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES parent(a)) ENGINE=InnoDB;

CREATE TABLE father(a INT PRIMARY KEY) ENGINE=InnoDB;
CREATE TABLE son(a INT PRIMARY KEY) ENGINE=InnoDB;

--source include/restart_mysqld.inc

RENAME TABLE parent TO mother, child to daughter;
RENAME TABLE father TO parent, son to child;

SHOW CREATE TABLE daughter;
SHOW CREATE TABLE child;

DROP TABLE daughter,mother,child,parent;
{code}
I started the 10.6 server using the following:
{code:sh}
./mtr --manual-gdb innodb.fk_upgrade
{code}
Then, in the middle of the execution, I switched the executable:
{noformat}
[Inferior 1 (process 1681520) exited normally]
(gdb) file /dev/shm/10.6fk/sql/mariadbd
Load new symbol table from "/dev/shm/10.6fk/sql/mariadbd"? (y or n) y
Reading symbols from /dev/shm/10.6fk/sql/mariadbd...
(gdb) run
{noformat}
First, the test would fail with the following result difference:
{code:diff}
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@
   PRIMARY KEY (`a`),
   CONSTRAINT `daughter_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`a`) REFERENCES `mother` (`a`)
 ) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=latin1
+Warnings:
+Note	1459	Upgrade required. Please do "REPAIR TABLE `daughter`" or dump/reload to fix it!
 SHOW CREATE TABLE child;
 Table	Create Table
 child	CREATE TABLE `child` (
{code}
With a rebuild after setting {{WITH_INNODB_LEGACY_FOREIGN_STORAGE:BOOL=OFF}} I got the following result difference (after removing {{innodb_sys_foreign}} and {{innodb_sys_foreign_cols}} from the startup parameters, to allow the server to start):
{code:diff}
@@ -9,8 +9,7 @@
 Table	Create Table
 daughter	CREATE TABLE `daughter` (
   `a` int(11) NOT NULL,
-  PRIMARY KEY (`a`),
-  CONSTRAINT `daughter_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`a`) REFERENCES `mother` (`a`)
+  PRIMARY KEY (`a`)
 ) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=latin1
 SHOW CREATE TABLE child;
 Table	Create Table
{code}
This proves what I suspected based on a quick read of the code: Because the code fails to delete old metadata on DDL operations, bogus {{FOREIGN KEY}} relations may be discovered.

