Some other failures include wrong results in gcol.innodb_virtual_basic and gcol.innodb_virtual_index (NULL instead of non-NULL values), and others.

I suspect this has something to do with the innodb side of the patch.

Following up on discussions, ptal at the Milestone 1 patch above (also in the updated draft PR https://github.com/MariaDB/server/pull/3487), [~marko], and let me know whether the SQL layer is sufficient, and if not, what else is needed.

Ideally the final patch should have some basic changes on the innodb side so that it contains tests showing that it works. This is the case with the current patch, but unfortunately the innodb changes suffer from some failures mentioned above. Can you take a look at these failures too and suggest fixes? Thanks.

I have found one issue in 

{code}
commit 97830d0633bdd578e130a2705d023e0a140d0440
Author: Yuchen Pei <ycp@mariadb.com>
Date:   Tue Feb 10 20:54:09 2026 +1100

    MDEV-24813 Signal full scan to storage engines, with innodb implementation
{code}


It adds this

{code:diff}
+int
+ha_innobase::extra_opt(
+/*===============*/
+       enum ha_extra_function operation,
+                          /*!< in: HA_EXTRA_FLUSH or some other flag */
+       ulong arg)
+{
+       switch (operation) {
+               /* TODO: ignoring LIMIT for now */
+       case HA_EXTRA_FULL_SCAN:
+               m_prebuilt->full_table_scan= true;
+               break;
+       default:/* Do nothing */
+               ;
+       }
+
+       return(0);
+}
{code}

But note that the original extra_opt() implementation in class handler calls extra():

{code:sql}
  virtual int extra_opt(enum ha_extra_function operation, ulong arg)
  { return extra(operation); }
{code}

Now, this no longer happens.
This causes {{gcol.innodb_virtual_index gcol.innodb_virtual_basic}} tests to fail. I am 
not sure why but if I change extra_opt() to call extra():

{code:diff}
+int
+ha_innobase::extra_opt(
+/*===============*/
+       enum ha_extra_function operation,
+                          /*!< in: HA_EXTRA_FLUSH or some other flag */
+       ulong arg)
+{
+       bool handled = false;
+       switch (operation) {
+       case HA_EXTRA_FULL_SCAN:
+               handled = true;
+               if (!m_prebuilt->skip_locked)
+                       m_prebuilt->full_table_scan = true;
+               break;
+       default:/* Do nothing */
+               ;
+       }
+
+        if (!handled) 
+          return extra(operation);
+
+       return(0);
+}
{code}
the problem goes away.

I debugged the scenario for {{gcol.innodb_virtual_basic}} and understood that
InnoDB doesn't set the prebuilt->read_just_key when it is being called with {{HA_EXTRA_KEYREAD}}
{code}
  inline int ha_start_keyread(uint idx)
  {
    DBUG_ASSERT(!keyread_enabled());
    keyread= idx;
    return extra_opt(HA_EXTRA_KEYREAD, idx);
  }
{code}

we use read_just_key to determine whether to read virtual column or not in {{row_search_mvcc()}}
{code}
bool    need_vrow = prebuilt->read_just_key
                && prebuilt->index->has_virtual();      
{code}

Current commit, after implementing suggestions from the Tuesday meeting:

{noformat}
8c49f784b50 upstream/bb-11.4-mdev-24813-v2 MDEV-24813 [wip] Add an innodb switch table_lock_on_full_scan
