only notable failures on buildbot are: innodb.avoid_deadlock_with_blocked (windows only), innodb.insert_into_empty (reverting to ER_DUP_ENTRY with ps protocol).

main.innodb_full_scan fails view protocol in x86-debian-12-fulltest-debug, but something as simple as the following hang with view protocol at the current 11.4 4d4f0ccea78102af5f396d4fdd33e196a85a276c but not the current main daf29b5e47fe511ce09c0cb9c803b8f76af1cfbb (is this a known bug?), and the innodb suite is not run with view protocol in the same builder, so I sourced no_view_protocol.inc in main.innodb_full_scan.

{code:sql}
--source include/have_innodb.inc
CREATE TABLE t (a INT PRIMARY KEY) ENGINE=InnoDB;
insert into t values (42);
BEGIN;
SELECT * FROM t LOCK IN SHARE MODE;  # hang
