Review input for DERIVED_CONDITION_PUSHDOWN:

So, before the patch we had this logic:
{code:sql}
if (optimizer_flag(OPTIMIZER_SWITCH_COND_PUSHDOWN_FOR_DERIVED))
{
  for (each tbl in select_lex->leaf_tables) {
    if (tbl->is_materialized_derived()) {
      // possibly do pushdown
      mysql_handle_single_derived(thd->lex, tbl, DT_OPTIMIZE);
    }
  }
}
else
  select_lex->handle_derived(thd->lex, DT_OPTIMIZE); // (2)
{code}

Assuming that call (2) handles elements of select_lex->leaf_tables which have is_materialized_derived()=true,
then any materialized derived child will have handle_derived(DT_OPTIMIZE)  called for it.

After the fix: consider a query:
{code:sql}
create table t1 (a int, b int);
insert into t1 select 1, seq from seq_1_to_10;

create table t2 (a int, b int);
insert into t2 select 1, seq from seq_1_to_10;

select 
  /*+ DERIVED_CONDITION_PUSHDOWN(TBL1) NO_DERIVED_CONDITION_PUSHDOWN(TBL2) */
  *
from 
  (select max(b) as maxb, a from t1 group by a) as TBL1,
  (select max(b) as maxb, a from t2 group by a) as TBL2
where TBL1.a<3 and TBL2.a<2;
{code}

Here, optimization will be done for the join inside TBL1 but not for the join inside TBL2. 
I wasn't able to observe any differences because of this, but I would prefer if this patch didn't make such changes.
Let all subqueries be optimized.

mysql-test/main/mdev-36106-derived-condition-pushdown-hint.result :
{code:js}
select json_extract(trace, '$.steps[1].join_optimization.steps[1].join_optimization.steps[0].condition_processing') from information_schema.optimizer_trace;
json_extract(trace, '$.steps[1].join_optimization.steps[1].join_optimization.steps[0].condition_processing')
{"condition": "HAVING", "original_condition": "max_c < 707 and (max_c > 300 or max_c < 135)", "steps": [{"transformation": "equality_propagation", "resulting_condition": "max_c < 707 and (max_c > 300 or max_c < 135)"}, {"transformation": "constant_propagation", "resulting_condition": "max_c < 707 and (max_c > 300 or max_c < 135)"}, {"transformation": "trivial_condition_removal", "resulting_condition": "max_c < 707 and (max_c > 300 or max_c < 135)"}]}
