{quote}
It seems to me that rewriting ORDER BY vcol_expr into ORDER BY vcol_field as described in MDEV-35615 can only help the third query
{quote}
I think it should help with both first and 3rd queries, whenever {{ORDER BY vcol_expr}} is encountered.
Note that the choice whether to use filesort is cost-based. If you have only 3 rows (and other indexes) the optimizer may still prefer to read +sort them even if a matching index is available. The situation gets worse when the index is not considered to be covering.    (The optimizer probably doesn't know that  INDEX(vcol_field) covers vcol_expr). 

I'll put better examples in the MDEV description.

