Both tests are very quick (take under 1 sec on my machine), but vec1.test is fairly big in size.
I think at least vec2-like test is definitely worth adding, but maybe we can replace the actual contents of vec1 with something generated and lose a second or two but make it small, it will be a good bargain.
Please note that the contents of both tests is taken from one of existing public benchmarks/examples (I don't remember now which, for my tests I called it gist_960_1K where 960 is the number of dimensions and 1K is the number of rows, which may give you the clue of where it comes from), so maybe it cannot be released with our code anyway due to licensing or something.

In my opinion the feature as of [bf34d4b9|https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/bf34d4b98afab8edf6600c43e6d56cb6694e58a9] can be pushed into the main branch and released with 12.1 RC, assuming the benchmark results were satisfactory.

As Sergei explained in the comments, the feature has no functional visibility to the user; performance characteristics, including recall, on realistic/standardized datasets was tested separately, as can be seen in the commit and JIRA comments, while measuring any of those on artificial data is pointless; so the feature testing here was focused on stability. 

I didn't get any failures specific to this task, and after applying the fix for MDEV-37063 / MDEV-37247 on top of the feature tree, I didn't observe any stability problems specific to vector search. The line coverage of the concurrent tests is approximately the same as in MTR, I consider it satisfactory:

