{noformat:title=[main-MDEV-35248] [42b21a807bf72386549f942872dc672e09822c67]}{noformat}

1. Compiled the Server code with MYROCKS SE enabled. 

2. Started the Server (Doner) with default location of data directory.
{code}
./sql/mysqld \
  --no-defaults \
  --basedir=$PWD \
  --datadir=$PWD/data \
  --log-error=$PWD/data/mysql.log \
  --socket=$PWD/data/mysql.sock \
  --port=10000 \
  --plugin-dir=/home/satish/WORKSPACE/server/local_clone/bld_clone-debug/plugin/clone\
  --plugin-load-add=mariadb_clone.so \
  --plugin-load-add=ha_rocksdb.so
{code}

3. Installed the clone Plugin and it was successful.
{code}
INSTALL PLUGIN clone SONAME 'mariadb_clone';
{code}

4. Installed MYROCKS plugin and it was successful.
{code}
install plugin rocksdb soname 'ha_rocksdb';
{code}

5. Created database "cloneTest" and created multiple tables for different SE.
{code}
create database cloneTest;
use cloneTest;

create table myisam_table (id int primary key, name varchar(50)) engine=myisam;
insert into myisam_table values (1, "myiasm_row1"),(2,"myiasm_row2");

create table csv_table (id int not null, name varchar(50) not null) engine=csv;
insert into csv_table values (1, "csv_row1"),(2,"csv_row2");

create table myrocks_table (id int primary key, name varchar(50)) engine=rocksdb;
insert into myrocks_table values (1, "myrocks_row1"),(2,"myrocks_row2");

create table myisam_m1(id int primary key, data varchar(50)) engine=myisam;
create table myisam_m2(id int primary key, data varchar(50)) engine=myisam;
insert into myisam_m1 values (1, "myisam_m1_row1"),(2,"myisam_m1_row2");
insert into myisam_m2 values (1, "myisam_m2_row1"),(2,"myisam_m2_row2");

create table myisam_merge(id int primary key, data varchar(50)) engine=mrg_myisam union=(myisam_m1,myisam_m2);

create table innodb_table (id int primary key, data varchar(50)) engine=innodb;
insert into innodb_table values (1, "innodb_row1"),(2,"innodb_row2");
{code}

6. Performed Local Clone.
{code}
CLONE LOCAL DATA DIRECTORY = '/home/satish/clone/data'
{code}

7. Killed the server and started the server again by providing the new location of data directory.
{code}
./sql/mysqld \
  --no-defaults \
  --basedir=$PWD \
  --datadir=/home/satish/clone/data \
  --log-error=/home/satish/clone/data/mysql.log \
  --socket=/home/satish/clone/data/mysql.sock \
  --port=10000 \
  --plugin-dir=/home/satish/WORKSPACE/server/local_clone/bld_clone-debug/plugin/clone\
  --plugin-load-add=mariadb_clone.so \
  --plugin-load-add=ha_rocksdb.so
{code}

8. Check all table list in cloneTest.
{code}
+---------------------+
| Tables_in_cloneTest |
+---------------------+
| csv_table           |
| innodb_table        |
| myisam_m1           |
| myisam_m2           |
| myisam_merge        |
| myisam_table        |
| myrocks_table       |
+---------------------+
{code}

9. Verified the data for each table and it was intact, except *myrocks_table *which was not accessible.
{code}
MariaDB [cloneTest]> select * from myrocks_table;
ERROR 1286 (42000): Unknown storage engine 'ROCKSDB'
{code}

10. Checking available plugins also does not show ROCKSDB.

11. Trying to reinstall the plugin gives error.
{code}
MariaDB [cloneTest]> install plugin rocksdb soname 'ha_rocksdb';
ERROR 1123 (HY000): Can't initialize function 'rocksdb'; Plugin initialization function failed.
{code}

12. Error logs had following information.
{code}
2025-08-08 12:06:35 3 [ERROR] RocksDB: Error opening instance, Status Code: 5, Status: IO error: lock : ./#rocksdb/LOCK: No locks available
2025-08-08 12:06:35 3 [ERROR] Plugin 'ROCKSDB' registration as a STORAGE ENGINE failed.
