[~svoj] there is conditional initialization in add_table_to_list():

{noformat}
  if (!ptr->is_pure_alias())
  {
    MDL_REQUEST_INIT(&ptr->mdl_request, MDL_key::TABLE, ptr->db.str,
                     ptr->table_name.str, mdl_type, MDL_TRANSACTION);
  }
{noformat}

It is required to track the state. Making it unconditionally means mdl_key_init() for pure alias. There is no good way to do it out of add_table_to_list() and then avoid accessing MDL when there is no need. Refactoring this deep can lead to serious algorithmic changes, but is not worth the goal (if there is no performance win).

[~svoj] There is a fix for TABLE_LIST::reset() and ctor initialization conflict:

{code}
2a8d889b544 (origin/bb-10.11-midenok, mariadb/bb-10.11-midenok, bb-10.11-midenok) MDEV-39184 Cleanup for MDL_NOT_INITIALIZED
8039d774161 MDEV-39184 TABLE_LIST C++-friendly initialization refactoring
{code}

[~svoj], [~sanja] please review.

